WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.025
A single run is a reading.

3
00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:05.125
A program needs three more things.

4
00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:09.588
First, the readings over time: which
findings were fixed, which came back,

5
00:00:09.588 --> 00:00:13.900
and which only seemed to disappear
because the run lost a connection.

6
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.088
Second, one finding per setting.

7
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:20.861
The Zero Trust Assessment's findings
have to line up with ScubaGear's, and,

8
00:00:20.861 --> 00:00:23.804
where the agency runs
AWS, with Security Hub's,

9
00:00:23.804 --> 00:00:27.862
so one setting under one control
is one finding with one owner.

10
00:00:27.862 --> 00:00:31.450
And third, every run sealed, so
an assessor can check months

11
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:35.038
later that the files are the
ones the tool and the kit wrote.

12
00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:39.695
In this module you'll compare two
runs, reconcile through the control,

13
00:00:39.695 --> 00:00:44.260
set a cadence, and seal an evidence
package, then break it on purpose.
